WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.690
- Do you like producing or acting better?

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.140
- I like both, honestly.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.440
But I definitely wanna do
more producing as well.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.140
Like it just feels...

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.970
You know, in life like, as you...

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:10.930
- A little bit of ownership?

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:11.950
- Yeah, exactly.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.349
- Well, and even collaborating though.

00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:16.380
So you were telling me, we
ran into each other years ago,

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.390
and I literally left going,

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:19.173
oh my God, I just met Jessie Spano!

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:21.507
I was freaking out, and it was crazy.

00:00:21.507 --> 00:00:23.450
- Meantime, I'm freaking
out probably over here.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.500
You're freaking out over there.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.693
'Cause like I'm obsessed
with your music, so.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.110
- Well, we had a freak
out moment together then.

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.450
But then it cut to, now we're here,

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.920
and you're doing "Saved
By The Bell" the reunion.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.460
So I think the reboot is so cool.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.130
I had Mario on and we
talked about it a bit.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:40.340
'Cause I already got really mad at him.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.173
- Why, tell me.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:42.006
- 'Cause he was the first
cast member to come on.

00:00:42.006 --> 00:00:44.510
And I was like, hey, I
knew the whole theme song.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.450
Like, I'm a really great jingle singer.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.370
I could have done the theme song.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.117
- You could have done it amazing.

00:00:50.117 --> 00:00:50.950
- Oh my God, I would have...

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.100
You have no idea, I
freaking saw every episode

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.440
at 10:00 AM every morning
in Texas, it's fine.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.290
So like, is that kind of cool

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.240
getting back, like so many years later?

00:00:59.273 --> 00:01:00.610
- Honestly, it's the best.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:03.510
Like the core four of us have
never stopped being in touch.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.960
We are friends, I know their children.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.610
I'm friends with their spouses.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:11.560
You know, so to then drop back in,

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.130
I remember sitting across from Mario,

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.160
like the first day of shooting at The Max.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:15.993
- At The Max!

00:01:15.993 --> 00:01:17.639
- Yeah.
- I love it.

00:01:17.639 --> 00:01:18.650
- And I'm sitting there
looking at this face

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:20.060
that I have known through the years.

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.450
We were truly children when we started.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:23.283
- I know!

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.877
- If someone had told me
then that I would see him

00:01:26.877 --> 00:01:30.630
this many years later
back as that character,

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.630
I wouldn't have believed it.

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.230
- I know, but it was such
a huge pop culture moment.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.910
Like few people are part
of something that massive,

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.180
that makes such an impact.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.890
- So my question that I asked him,

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:43.420
so AC Slater is now the athletic director.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:45.330
- Yes.
- So who is Jessie Spano?

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:48.930
- So Jessie, in perfect Jessie Spano form,

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.452
is the guidance counselor, okay?

00:01:50.452 --> 00:01:51.543
- Oh my god, I love it.

00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:53.390
- 'Cause like even back in the day,

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.234
with the OG friends, she
was always the advice giver.

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.920
She was always wanting to help people.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.480
And she was an advocate for
so many different causes

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.620
and her son, Jamie is a student here.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.530
So she's a bit of a helicopter parent,

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.953
and thus comedy ensues.

